// ADR 0073 D1, the other direction: what a `k(v)` resume delivers crosses the same
// one-`i64` seam. Two unrelated checks already stopped a USE of a ref-returning op —
// the borrow layer's fail-closed source rule, and ADR 0072's `FITS` — but each fired
// several lines from the declaration that made the use impossible, and either could
// be re-scoped for its own reasons. The rule is stated once, here.
effect Io {
    get() -> &i64;
}
fn main() -> i64 {
    0
}
